# Explicit text normalization: text is stored with LF in Git and checked out
# with LF on every platform, including Windows (Node, TypeScript, ESLint and
# Git itself all handle LF there). Content is UTF-8 and is never re-encoded.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must keep LF regardless of platform.
*.sh    text eol=lf
# Released schema migrations are checksummed (the runtime also normalizes CRLF before hashing).
*.sql   text eol=lf

# Windows-native script formats keep CRLF so cmd.exe and Windows PowerShell 5.1
# read them predictably. PowerShell files must also be UTF-8 *with* BOM
# (see .editorconfig); a BOM-less .ps1 is read as ANSI by PowerShell 5.1.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.psm1  text eol=crlf
*.psd1  text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf

# Imported canonical authority: exact byte copies of the Founder-local sources
# (see docs/authority/company-architecture/AUTHORITY_IMPORT_MANIFEST.md). Their
# Markdown hard line breaks (two trailing spaces) are content, so Git's
# whitespace checks are off for these files only. Git also never normalizes
# their line endings (-text): the bytes stored are the source bytes (all LF).
docs/authority/company-architecture/*/*.md -text -whitespace

# Binary content: never normalized, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.7z    binary
*.gz    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.wav   binary
*.sqlite  binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.db    binary

# D1: the one-time copy of the ratified brand authority's app icon (QANDEEL App, I-08B2.5) is byte-exact:
# its SHA-256 is the provenance (packaging/windows/assets/ICON_PROVENANCE.json); Git never normalizes it.
packaging/windows/assets/source/*.svg -text
